###Project1 - Group 6: Sequence Assemblies and Quality Control (Mentor: Matt Loose)

##Introduction

Group 6 focused on studying genomic variations in microorganism strains. Various genetic changes were introduced, but their precise locations were unknown. This project aimed to create assemblies to identify these changes using predominantly long-read data.
This repository includes the scripts for:

Generating assemblies from long and short reads.
Performing quality control on assemblies.
Visualization and annotation of assembled genomes.

#Features of the Pipeline

Code for Generating Assemblies
Short-read assembly
Long-read assembly
Hybrid (short + long) read assembly
Quality Control Tools
BUSCO: Benchmarking Universal Single-Copy Orthologs.
QUAST: Quality Assessment Tool for Genome Assemblies.
Visualization and Annotation Tools
Flye: Long-read genome assembler.
Prokka: Rapid genome annotation tool.
Genovi: Visualization of genome annotations.
